{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1788222942,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"**CONCRETE_BREAK_FOUND**\n\n`scripts/generate-live-proof.js` loads environment variables from a **non‑existent file** (`.env.gates`) instead of the standard `.env` used by the rest of the platform. Consequently, when the script is run (e.g., after setting `LIVE_TRADING=true` in a real `.env`), it still reports the environment as `PAPER` because the intended variables are never read.\n\n* Evidence of the faulty load line:  \n  ```js\n  require('dotenv').config({ path: path.join(__dirname, '..', '.env.gates') });\n  ```  \n  (see `scripts/generate-live-proof.js` line 274【open_file†L274-L274】).\n\n* The repository contains a proper `.env` example (`config/.env.example`) but **no `.env.gates` file** (search for `.env.gates` finds only documentation, not an actual file)【search†L1-L1】.\n\n* Demonstration of the break: creating a real `.env` with `LIVE_TRADING=true` and executing the script still yields `Env: PAPER` because the script never reads that file【run_check†L1-L31】.\n\n* The script also falls back to `unknown` for the git commit (irrelevant to the env bug) but the critical failure is the missing environment data, which can cause the live‑proof page to mis‑represent the system’s operational mode.\n\n**Impact:** Any automation that relies on `scripts/generate-live-proof.js` to publish the live‑proof page will incorrectly claim the system is in paper mode, potentially hiding live‑trading status and breaking compliance monitoring. This is a concrete, reproducible failure that is not covered by the existing test suite.","tool_calls":[],"tool_call_id":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":39661,"completion_tokens":443,"total_tokens":40104,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4908},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":78}},"warning":null,"reasoning_summary":null}